<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vishnu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vishnu is one of the principal gods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hinduism</a>, worshipped as the preserver of the universe and, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnavism</a>, as the supreme being. He is believed to descend to earth in avatars, among them the boar Varaha, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama">Rama</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a>, to restore cosmic order. His worship spread across South and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, where kings from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> identified themselves with him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vishnu.jpg" alt="Vishnu" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Manaku of Guler · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vishnu_from_Gita_Govinda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
